Test Case: other_bypass_platform_safety_checks_on_user_schedule_removed
================================================================================

Initial Error (Step 3):
Error: Attempt to get attribute from null value
  on azapi.tf line 52, in resource "azapi_resource" "this":
  52:       type         = identity.value.type
     ├────────────────
     │ identity.value is null
This value is null, so it does not have any attributes.

Fix Process:

Attempt 1:
- Problem Analysis: The dynamic identity block uses `can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity)` which returns true even when identity is null, causing an error when trying to access identity.value.type on a null value
- Fix Method: Change the condition from `can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity)` to `module.replicator.azapi_header.identity != null` to properly check for null values
- Changes Made: Updated azapi.tf line 50 to use `module.replicator.azapi_header.identity != null` instead of `can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity)`
- Result: Success - plan now executes without errors

Drift Analysis:
All detected drifts match acceptable patterns from acceptable_drift_patterns.md:
1. Resource-level attributes (ignore_null_property, type, output, locks, replace_triggers_external_values, sensitive_body_version, timeouts) - Section 1 acceptable
2. Body changes appear to be computed/optional fields being removed when ignore_null_property=true - Section 2 acceptable pattern

Proceeding to apply changes to verify idempotency.

